==Old English==

===Etymology 1===
{{PIE root|ang|h₁eḱ}}
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*ehwaz|t=horse}}, from {{inh|ang|ine-pro|*h₁éḱwos|t=horse}}. Cognate with {{cog|osx|ehuskalk|t=horse-rider}}, {{cog|goh|eha-}} (in personal names), {{cog|non|jór}}, {{cog|got|*𐌰𐌹𐍈𐍃}}. The Indo-European root is also the source of {{cog|la|equus}}, {{cog|ae|𐬀𐬯𐬞𐬀}}, {{cog|fa|اسب}}, {{cog|sa|अश्व|tr=áśva}}, {{cog|xcl|էշ|t=donkey}}, {{cog|xto|yuk}}, {{cog|txb|yakwe}}, {{cog|ine-bsl-pro|*áśwāˀ}} ({{cog|lt|ašvà}}), {{cog|sga|ech}} ({{cog|ga|each}}).

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|ang|/eo̯h/|[eo̯x]}}

====Noun====
{{ang-noun|m|g2=n}}

# {{lb|ang|poetic}} [[horse]], [[steed]]

